    {'padas': ["athemā atistutaya ityācakṣate | api vā saṃpratyaya eva syāt | māhābhāgyād devatāyāḥ | so'gnimeva prathamamāha |", 'tvamagne dyubhistvamāśuśukṣaṇiḥ |', 'iti yathaitasminsūkte |', 'na hi tvadāre nimiṣaśca neśe |', 'iti varuṇasya |', 'athaiṣendrasya'], 'num': '|| 1 ||', 'gloss': 'These are called "over-praises" (atistuti), or simply plain statements, from the greatness of the deity. First of Agni: "you, Agni, from the heavens…"; of Varuṇa: "not even the twinkling of an eye is far from you". Now one of Indra.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '13.2 · Indra beyond measure'},
    {'padas': ['yaddyāva indra te śataṃ śataṃ bhūmīruta syuḥ |', 'na tvā vajrintsahasraṃ sūryā anu na jātamaṣṭa rodasī ||', 'yadi ta indra śataṃ divaḥ śataṃ bhūmayaḥ pratimānāni syurna tvā vajrintsahasramapi sūryā na dyāvāpṛthivyāvapyabhyaśnuvītāmiti |', 'athaiṣādityasya'], 'num': '|| 2 ||', 'gloss': 'Ṛgveda 8.70.5: if you had a hundred heavens and a hundred earths, Indra, a thousand suns could not equal you, nor heaven and earth. Now one of the sun.', 'prose': True},
